Expert Prompt for Perplexity
Generate a complete backend API in Python (FastAPI preferred) for a conversational timesheet chatbot.

Use SQL Server as the database and define two tables: OracleTimesheet and MarsTimesheet. These represent two systems, and the user must choose one before starting to fill the timesheet using a prompt.

The chatbot should be fully conversational and support multi-turn interactions. The client will only have a chat interface and will send two parameters to the API: email and user_prompt.

The API should handle all logic internally and return a ready-to-render response, including HTML-formatted tables for timesheet summaries.

The chatbot must support the following advanced features:

Conversational input across multiple steps

User can fill timesheets for multiple dates, multiple systems, and multiple task codes/project codes in a single prompt or across multiple prompts

Timesheet entry for one day, multiple days, or full week (Monday to Friday)

View existing timesheet entries

Ask for project codes before filling timesheet

Modify pre-filled timesheet entries

Copy last week’s timesheet and make changes

Save timesheet entries with validation (e.g., hours must be numeric, date must be valid)

Handle natural language inputs like “yesterday”, “tomorrow”, “2 hours on Mars project”, “same as last Monday”

The API should:

Maintain session context per user (based on email)

Validate and parse user input intelligently

Return structured responses with conversational text and HTML tables

Include all business logic and validation in the API itself

🔧 LLM Integration: Use Ollama 3.2 1B as the backend language model. Assume Ollama is installed locally and accessible via direct Python calls.

Do not use generic HTTP API calls. Instead, use the native Python interface:

python
ollama.chat(
    model=self.model_name,
    messages=[{"role": "user", "content": "Hello"}],
    options={"temperature": 0.7, "num_ctx": 4096}
)
